})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550868} {:answer/id #uuid "b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550870} {:answer/id #uuid "d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550860} :answer-field/id #uuid "b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343391" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=3{x}^{2}$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)={x}^{3}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and we are already given the coefficients for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ \nTherefore, the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}({\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nt))\\text{d}t \\\\ [{t}^{3}]_{0}^{x} & ∼[{\\pi }^{2}t]_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nt)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ {x}^{3} & ∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550693} {:answer/id #uuid "86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550708} {:answer/id #uuid "dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550966} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551043} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550966} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/math-academy-id "q-144400" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v).$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡u=1-{cos}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡u & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-(-\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{6}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b570f2-170f-50b9-b0a5-9563089e0914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12)\\,\\mathbf i+(-4)\\,\\mathbf j+(-18)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551553} {:answer/id #uuid "85d95e24-11f1-5424-b411-e0cba95ba1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{3}{7})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{1}{7})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{3}{7})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551566} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d64b4c-f8eb-5e52-a731-c64e6c9515d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{3}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{3}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551579} {:answer/id #uuid "b8cf17ec-9cf4-5d4b-ac5b-642ccc70904b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551581} {:answer/id #uuid "eddd4ced-d849-5ca7-ab21-5aa50e4a8fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{30}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{10}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{24}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8cf17ec-9cf4-5d4b-ac5b-642ccc70904b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551581} :answer-field/id #uuid "c14bbab2-5183-5313-8025-08879f6edb60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01b80278-13c1-5bc7-888c-457bedd82092" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇g(x,y,z)$ at the point $(1,3,1)$ if $g(x,y,z)=- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x + y + z)(- y z)-(- x y z)(3)}{(3 x + y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{y z \\left(y + z\\right)}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x + y + z)(- x z)-(- x y z)(1)}{(3 x + y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{x z \\left(3 x + z\\right)}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x + y + z)(- x y)-(- x y z)(1)}{(3 x + y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{x y \\left(3 x + y\\right)}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(\\frac{3 x y z}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{y z}{3 x + y + z})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{x y z}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{x z}{3 x + y + z})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{x y z}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{x y}{3 x + y + z})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ ∇g(1,3,1) & =(\\frac{(7)(-3)-(-3)(3)}{(7)^2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{(7)(-1)-(-3)(1)}{(7)^2})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{(7)(-3)-(-3)(1)}{(7)^2})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f20dac-6288-5051-a0c9-656192ea317e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{54}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{18}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{18}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551535} {:answer/id #uuid "1b82d1e6-c06d-5bc5-a3be-ca74e8368591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{6}{11})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{18}{11})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{6}{11})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551539} {:answer/id #uuid "2beb0246-9a96-5b86-b925-3ee4afed1adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12)\\,\\mathbf i+(-216)\\,\\mathbf j+(-48)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551541} {:answer/id #uuid "30d13711-2fa2-5805-aef5-71db8eb39744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551545} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e4497f-d6d4-5ce0-a5a1-5acd3a94ffb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{120}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{180}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{84}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30d13711-2fa2-5805-aef5-71db8eb39744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551545} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf24e375-8a4c-5062-b9e8-dd5c1bf1791d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2d2b5e18-84ca-5425-a8f7-9933f3d81196" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇g(x,y,z)$ at the point $(3,1,3)$ if $g(x,y,z)=- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - y + z)(- 2 y z)-(- 2 x y z)(3)}{(3 x - y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2 y z \\left(y - z\\right)}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - y + z)(- 2 x z)-(- 2 x y z)(-1)}{(3 x - y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 x z \\left(3 x + z\\right)}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - y + z)(- 2 x y)-(- 2 x y z)(1)}{(3 x - y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 x y \\left(3 x - y\\right)}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(\\frac{6 x y z}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{2 y z}{3 x - y + z})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{2 x y z}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{2 x z}{3 x - y + z})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{2 x y z}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{2 x y}{3 x - y + z})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ ∇g(3,1,3) & =(\\frac{(11)(-6)-(-18)(3)}{(11)^2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{(11)(-18)-(-18)(-1)}{(11)^2})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{(11)(-6)-(-18)(1)}{(11)^2})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "326a1a4f-342f-55b4-a110-a2709831b255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{11}{16})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551546} {:answer/id #uuid "5e3bfb05-0026-500e-ab07-b20fa3d7a282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{7}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{7}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{13}{16})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551555} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3b866f-b033-5d4a-960c-12a16bdfb0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(90)\\,\\mathbf i+(9)\\,\\mathbf j+(-99)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551562} {:answer/id #uuid "890840ec-d66a-5ea2-a525-97e6db70ac5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{3}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{1}{16})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551567} {:answer/id #uuid "b54a31e3-2b50-5c38-88f2-32aebf4915c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{3}{4})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "326a1a4f-342f-55b4-a110-a2709831b255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{11}{16})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551546} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab5196fb-11c8-5508-80c7-18d7ea226d31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "475d0eee-bd08-5379-9e3a-cbd39068cbc3" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇g(x,y,z)$ at the point $(-1,-3,1)$ if $g(x,y,z)=- \\frac{3 x y z}{- 2 x - 3 y + z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- \\frac{3 x y z}{- 2 x - 3 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(- 2 x - 3 y + z)(- 3 y z)-(- 3 x y z)(-2)}{(- 2 x - 3 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3 y z \\left(3 y - z\\right)}{\\left(2 x + 3 y - z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- \\frac{3 x y z}{- 2 x - 3 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(- 2 x - 3 y + z)(- 3 x z)-(- 3 x y z)(-3)}{(- 2 x - 3 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3 x z \\left(2 x - z\\right)}{\\left(2 x + 3 y - z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- \\frac{3 x y z}{- 2 x - 3 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(- 2 x - 3 y + z)(- 3 x y)-(- 3 x y z)(1)}{(- 2 x - 3 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3 x y \\left(2 x + 3 y\\right)}{\\left(2 x + 3 y - z\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{6 x y z}{\\left(- 2 x - 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{3 y z}{- 2 x - 3 y + z})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{9 x y z}{\\left(- 2 x - 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{3 x z}{- 2 x - 3 y + z})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{3 x y z}{\\left(- 2 x - 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{3 x y}{- 2 x - 3 y + z})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ ∇g(-1,-3,1) & =(\\frac{(12)(9)-(-9)(-2)}{(12)^2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{(12)(3)-(-9)(-3)}{(12)^2})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{(12)(-9)-(-9)(1)}{(12)^2})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{11}{16})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{11}{16})\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05505486-92c7-55a4-9cb3-d01cdfa3a238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{45}{64})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{75}{128})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{57}{128})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551534} {:answer/id #uuid "ab289eb6-ba72-5080-9b39-a3d30df93602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{27}{64})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{21}{128})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{39}{128})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551576} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f42c0b-0803-5b4d-8016-ffcfa69893e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{9}{16})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{3}{8})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{3}{8})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551588} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b6ffbe-06e6-5a8e-aa0d-15175a4f5276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-108)\\,\\mathbf i+(-42)\\,\\mathbf j+(-78)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551590} {:answer/id #uuid "e84af700-5850-5c73-acbb-9a21f7272a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{64})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{27}{128})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{9}{128})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab289eb6-ba72-5080-9b39-a3d30df93602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{27}{64})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{21}{128})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{39}{128})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551576} :answer-field/id #uuid "14b7b09b-52da-5d72-b8df-bfa64684203c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "74938ef6-c9c2-59ba-827d-91ac5ff5232a" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇g(x,y,z)$ at the point $(-2,-3,-3)$ if $g(x,y,z)=\\frac{x y z}{2 x + 3 y + z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x y z}{2 x + 3 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(2 x + 3 y + z)(y z)-(x y z)(2)}{(2 x + 3 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{y z \\left(3 y + z\\right)}{\\left(2 x + 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x y z}{2 x + 3 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(2 x + 3 y + z)(x z)-(x y z)(3)}{(2 x + 3 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x z \\left(2 x + z\\right)}{\\left(2 x + 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{x y z}{2 x + 3 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(2 x + 3 y + z)(x y)-(x y z)(1)}{(2 x + 3 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x y \\left(2 x + 3 y\\right)}{\\left(2 x + 3 y + z\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{2 x y z}{\\left(2 x + 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{y z}{2 x + 3 y + z})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{3 x y z}{\\left(2 x + 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{x z}{2 x + 3 y + z})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{x y z}{\\left(2 x + 3 y + z\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{x y}{2 x + 3 y + z})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ ∇g(-2,-3,-3) & =(\\frac{(-16)(9)-(-18)(2)}{(-16)^2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{(-16)(6)-(-18)(3)}{(-16)^2})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{(-16)(6)-(-18)(1)}{(-16)^2})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{27}{64})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{21}{128})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{39}{128})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{27}{64})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{21}{128})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{39}{128})\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d55087-53de-5def-b995-b769126d00f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{6})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551563} {:answer/id #uuid "8d95b908-a2f2-59f4-aaca-fa9ce8ef8b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6)\\,\\mathbf i+(30)\\,\\mathbf j+(30)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551569} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d497b4-435f-5624-a8cc-86c18fe21fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{1}{6})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551587} {:answer/id #uuid "df4d1565-00b7-563a-8e03-f75c2a4a977d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{6})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{7}{6})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551589} {:answer/id #uuid "e47b5c86-36b9-58a9-bb61-fa06357f423b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathbf j+(1)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d55087-53de-5def-b995-b769126d00f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{6})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551563} :answer-field/id #uuid "8215a9cc-2670-5708-bd8e-57a5e6c7615b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8b44dc16-f32d-574a-a1bc-0e76d52e0a5c" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇g(x,y,z)$ at the point $(3,2,1)$ if $g(x,y,z)=\\frac{x y z}{3 x - 2 y + z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x y z}{3 x - 2 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - 2 y + z)(y z)-(x y z)(3)}{(3 x - 2 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{y z \\left(2 y - z\\right)}{\\left(3 x - 2 y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x y z}{3 x - 2 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - 2 y + z)(x z)-(x y z)(-2)}{(3 x - 2 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x z \\left(3 x + z\\right)}{\\left(3 x - 2 y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{x y z}{3 x - 2 y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - 2 y + z)(x y)-(x y z)(1)}{(3 x - 2 y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x y \\left(3 x - 2 y\\right)}{\\left(3 x - 2 y + z\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3 x y z}{\\left(3 x - 2 y + z\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{y z}{3 x - 2 y + z})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{2 x y z}{\\left(3 x - 2 y + z\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{x z}{3 x - 2 y + z})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{x y z}{\\left(3 x - 2 y + z\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{x y}{3 x - 2 y + z})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ ∇g(3,2,1) & =(\\frac{(6)(2)-(6)(3)}{(6)^2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{(6)(3)-(6)(-2)}{(6)^2})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{(6)(6)-(6)(1)}{(6)^2})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{1}{6})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{1}{6})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{5}{6})\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad87764-6044-5767-902d-f845c340fce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ or $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551881} {:answer/id #uuid "7236c074-3016-5112-a3b9-0ad8989ea929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-12$ or $-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551936} {:answer/id #uuid "9133a202-35d2-56e1-8e7d-2d811e679fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-18$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552019} {:answer/id #uuid "b0458107-3a29-5b00-817a-03a49afcbbfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ or $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552090} {:answer/id #uuid "e42a61a8-e821-58ec-be90-1c90c3e1e586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ or $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ad87764-6044-5767-902d-f845c340fce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ or $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551881} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7cd6986-58f2-5df8-9623-61bd4f8f7c74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fd09d79-cd92-571a-b908-4f0df92196ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-154703" :question/problem "If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=5,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=3-\\frac{2}{3}y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-\\frac{2}{3}y| & =5 \\\\ 3-\\frac{2}{3}y & =5 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $-\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3}y & =2 \\\\ (-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}y) & =(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (2) \\\\ (\\cancel{-\\frac{3}{2}})\\cdot (\\cancel{-\\frac{2}{3}}y) & =-\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ y & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=-(3-\\frac{2}{3}y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-\\frac{2}{3}y| & =5 \\\\ -(3-\\frac{2}{3}y) & =5 \\\\ -3+\\frac{2}{3}y & =5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y & =8 \\\\ (\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}y) & =(\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (8) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{3}{2}})\\cdot (\\cancel{\\frac{2}{3}}y) & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\ y & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-3$ and $y=12.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552028} :answer-field/id #uuid "3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551804} :answer-field/id #uuid "43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-325842" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{7}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{24}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that both $u$ and $v$ lie in the first quadrant, then\n\n| $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} $\\sqrt{3}\\,+\\,$ {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $50$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive, we take\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{24}{25})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+(\\frac{7}{25})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\sqrt{3}}{50}+\\frac{7}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\sqrt{3}+7}{50}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4692ff53-10f8-5d92-a62c-7ea8c8eb0b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551838} {:answer/id #uuid "85e69bf9-0ffa-5440-9692-3b79b4593ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551986} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552050} {:answer/id #uuid "a82aa644-63bf-5607-827a-5038ebc9e460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552067} {:answer/id #uuid "d741e5c8-f214-5380-b086-fc6bdd2df65d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552050} :answer-field/id #uuid "4db31d4f-92dd-5a4c-a9aa-c0b389b1913c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119581" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}-b}{26},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡u=1-{cos}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡u & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{13})(-\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{12}{13})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{26}+\\frac{12\\sqrt{3}}{26} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\sqrt{3}-5}{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=12,b=5,$ and $a+b=17.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "196dbf90-694f-56e1-bd9a-bacffff31ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551718} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca12552-8ad4-5d6a-8884-8f4afde5830a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5,\\, & 0<y<0.2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551849} {:answer/id #uuid "52cef4e5-3e19-5e35-bee0-384a657d1c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5y,\\, & 0<y<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551858} {:answer/id #uuid "a623ad96-993c-5f91-994d-d43006007fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552064} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e7845f-1c6b-5825-bbe7-1626dc1077e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5,\\, & 0<y<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "196dbf90-694f-56e1-bd9a-bacffff31ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551718} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bffd42c-4c16-5c26-a4d3-ff06e8bcf1b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1f799a56-7472-58ef-998d-84e22fb88853" :question/math-academy-id "q-110126" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{4},\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=1-{X}^{5},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=1-{X}^{5}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/05/05534475aecc1d0ebad2234f1259d1b6fd1c6183e47ad763f17c87c5fdb06afb.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-{X}^{5}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-{X}^{5}\\le y-1) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge (1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}((1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot {f}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot {f}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot 5{((1-y)^{1/5})}^{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "354f21b2-96ab-5d34-8629-17b1cd8d23d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551791} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee3cf3b-86e3-5e57-83f5-b5451cd4c7b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551893} {:answer/id #uuid "800e78fd-bc77-5f21-8b03-8b51fc29c534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551970} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ccdf0e-7384-5c78-bdab-6715b3b614a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552133} {:answer/id #uuid "f270c863-ecf9-5d37-bac9-47ebceb975b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "354f21b2-96ab-5d34-8629-17b1cd8d23d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551791} :answer-field/id #uuid "3231d9e1-5db0-532b-9d06-68eafedeb402" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "226b9b94-926b-577f-834a-35ff659d1159" :question/math-academy-id "q-102338" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $15{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 4+(-15)\\cdot 3}{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-45}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{25} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n15{x}_{2}=15\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})=-3.\n$$"}]
